[32m+[m[32m## Terms used here[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Keeper**: the person running the faucet. The keeper signs in through the padlock icon in the header (the "door") to connect the wallet, close the spring for maintenance and see the dashboard.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Keeper phrase**: a secret phrase of six random dictionary words (Diceware) that opens the door. It is never stored anywhere. Only its SHA-256 hash is set as `KEEPER_HASH`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Wallet**: the Lightning wallet that pays out. Connect it through the keeper door using [NWC](https://nwc.dev/) (for example an [Alby Hub](https://albyhub.com/)) or LNbits. The connection is stored encrypted in the database, not in environment variables.[m
